<title>USA: Sciclone buys stock from resigning chairman.</title>
<headline>Sciclone buys stock from resigning chairman.</headline>
<dateline>SAN MATEO, Calif. 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>SciClone Pharmaceuticals Inc said Friday it bought 1.88 million shares of its common stock for $5.95 million from its resigning chairman Thomas Moore.</p>
<p>Sciclone said its board elected Jere Goyan, a former U.S. Food and Drug Administration commissioner and currently president and chief operating officer of Alteon Inc, to replace Moore, who resigned effective immediately.</p>
<p>The company said it has the right to repurchase shares from Moore at a fixed discount rate.</p>
